      "description": "The hk@X.Y.Z pkl package that hk.pkl imports (amends + Builtins lines) must move together with the hk pin in mise.toml [tools] and mise.lock – the package provides the builtin step definitions the binary executes. The mise manager owns mise.toml + mise.lock; this manager keeps hk.pkl in the SAME update: same depName, datasource and currentValue as the mise manager's hk dep, so Renovate folds both into one branch and one PR bumps all three files. Two matchStrings because each import line carries the version twice (path segment and hk@X# marker) and both occurrences must be rewritten – the same invariant bump-hk.sh enforces for manual bumps. The CI check catches partial desyncs regardless: mise install --locked errors when mise.toml and mise.lock disagree.",
      "managerFilePatterns": [
        "/^hk\\.pkl$/"
      ],
